{% icon id="healing-shield" size=32 /%}Never run short of troops again. The **Recruit and tools** {% term id="plugin" %}plugin{% /term %} keeps each castle's troops and {% term id="tool" %}tools{% /term %} at the stock you set. When a castle has fewer than your target, the bot orders more from that castle's barracks or workshop.

{% terms_on_page /%}

It pays only with coins and resources, never with {% term id="ruby" %}rubies{% /term %}. Use it to refill your armies and siege tools after attacks without opening the game.

## How it works {% #how-it-works %}

1. A few minutes after your bot signs in, it reads the stock of every castle in your targets.
2. It counts what each castle holds: troops and tools at home, in production, in the queue, and out on marches.
3. If a castle holds fewer than your target, the bot orders the difference. Each order holds at most the **Per order** amount.
4. It orders only when the barracks or workshop has a free queue slot. It never unlocks a slot with rubies.
5. Before each order, it checks your coin and {% term id="resource-floor" %}resource floors{% /term %}. If an order would take you below a floor, it waits.
6. When the order in production finishes, the bot checks again. If nothing is in production, it checks again in about 15 minutes.

## Set your targets {% #targets %}

**Troop targets** and **Tool targets** are tables. Choose **Add row** and fill in every column:

- **Castle** is the castle that keeps the stock.
- **Troop** or **Tool** is what to keep. The list shows only troops paid with coins, and only tools paid with coins or resources.
- **Stock** is how many the castle should hold.
- **Per order** is the most the bot orders at one time. A tool order holds at most 80.

The castle list is empty until your bot has signed in once. Start the bot, wait for it to sign in, then come back to add rows.

{% aside type="caution" id="toolsmith-overlap" %}
The [Toolsmith](/modules/refinery-toolsmith/) {% term id="module" %}module{% /term %} does the same job for tools. Don't give both modules a target for the same tool.
{% /aside %}

## Keep coins and resources in reserve {% #floors %}

**Keep at least this many coins** is your coin floor. The bot never orders if the order would leave your account with fewer coins. The default is 100,000.

**Keep at least this much of each resource** is your resource floor. It applies to each resource in the castle that pays, such as wood and stone. The default is 0.

## Test with a dry run {% #dry-run %}

Turn on **Log only: write the orders to the log instead of sending them** to see what the bot would do. The bot writes each order to your {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %} and sends nothing to the game. Read the [Logs](/war-room/logs/) page, check the orders, then turn the switch off.

