{% settings plugin="recruitTools" /%}

## Read the status {% #status %}

The {% ui key="client:module.status" /%} card on the module page tells you what the plugin is doing now:

- **Every target is met.** The bot waits until a stock drops below its target.
- **The production queue is full.** The bot waits for a free slot.
- **Ordering** an item **would take you under your coin floor.** The bot waits until your coins are above the floor again.
- **Not enough resources to order** an item. The bot waits until the castle has resources above your floor.
- **A castle in your targets isn't on this account, or isn't known yet.** Check the castle in the row. The bot tries again on its next check.
- An item **can't be ordered with coins or resources, so it is skipped.** Pick a different troop or tool.

## Heal the wounded {% #heal %}

The **Heal troops** tab heals wounded troops in the castles you pick, up to the amount you set for each castle.

- It heals only troops the hospital heals with coins. It never heals a troop that costs rubies.
- It checks every castle in **Castles to heal in**, every 10 minutes unless you change **Check every**. It skips a castle with nobody wounded or a full hospital.
- It stops before an order would take your coins below **Keep at least this many coins**, or your spending this run above **Spend at most this many coins per run**.
- With **Ask the alliance for help** on, it asks your alliance to speed up a batch once.
- A castle without a hospital is never entered. You see a warning, and your list stays as you saved it.

**Recruit and tools** has the same **Ask the alliance for help** choice for the barracks.

## Related errors {% #errors %}

- [PLUGIN_OPTION_CASTLE](/errors/#plugin-option-castle) means a row names a castle that isn't on this account.
- [PLUGIN_OPTION_ITEM](/errors/#plugin-option-item) means a row names an item that isn't in the list.
- [PLUGIN_OPTION_ROWS](/errors/#plugin-option-rows) means a table has too many rows.
